{"uncertainty": 0.15, "outcome": "rtl_bug", "artifacts": [{"kind": "root_cause_analysis", "title": "uart_tx root cause: in-flight frame corrupted by a start pulse while busy", "summary": "Requirement [requirement:req-d10c4df532]. Observation: triage reproduced the failure, with 1 of 4 checks failed and $finish reached at 546000 [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e2] [run:run-0002]. VeriTriage labelled it unknown_failure at only 30% confidence, with 'Likely RTL bug' as its top hypothesis [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e1] [run:run-0001]. I treat that label as one candidate, not as the conclusion. Defect: the approved RTL [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1] has an unconditional 'if (start) hold <= data;' statement outside the state case. The file's own header says 'A start pulse while a frame is in flight is ignored.' Incorrectness: in START, DATA and STOP this statement overwrites the frame's holding register, which breaks that header requirement. Causality: the DATA state takes each next bit from hold[bit_idx+1]. A start pulse during bit n therefore makes bits n+1..7 come from the new data, so the received byte differs from the byte that was sent. Start, stop and idle bits are not affected, which fits a single failed check out of four. Fix direction, to be confirmed by review: load hold only in IDLE, which the IDLE branch already does. Ranked hypotheses: (1) rtl_bug. Refuting evidence would be the repro below passing on this RTL, or failing on RTL where the stray load is removed. (2) testbench_bug, rejected. The expected byte comes from the stimulus and the 8N1 framing, not from RTL output, and the checks of the untouched start, stop and idle bits pass. Refuting evidence would be the repro also failing on clean RTL. (3) infrastructure, rejected. The run built and reached $finish with a counted verdict [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e2], so it did not crash or time out. Refuting evidence would be a different result after a clean rebuild with no other change. (4) spec_ambiguity, rejected. The design's header clause states the required behaviour explicitly. Refuting evidence would be a governing specification that allows reload while busy. Review: the existing review record covers the fixture as reviewed in the repository [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.e1]. An independent review of this analysis is still required."}], "files": [{"path": "tb/uart_tx_reload_while_busy_repro_tb.v", "kind": "testbench", "title": "Self-checking repro: start pulse during an in-flight frame must be ignored", "summary": "Self-checking repro for the defect in [artifact:prj-d4a591eb4b.design-under-investigation.a1]. It drives three 8N1 frames with CLKS_PER_BIT=4 and samples each bit at its middle cycle. Frame 1 sends 0xA5 without disturbance. Frame 2 sends 0x3C and pulses start with data 0xC3 during data bit 3. Frame 3 sends 0x5A. In total it makes 13 checks: start bit, received byte, stop bit and return to idle for every frame, plus busy during the injected pulse. Expected values come from the stimulus and the framing rule, not from RTL output. It is expected to fail only the frame-2 byte check on this RTL and to pass on RTL that ignores start while busy, consistent with [evidence:prj-d4a591eb4b.triage.e2]. It prints one NIRMAAN-SIM verdict line with the plusarg nonce just before $finish.", "entry": "uart_tx_reload_while_busy_repro_tb"}], "tool_runs": ["run-0001", "run-0002"], "claims": ["The repro testbench is expected to fail exactly one check (frame 2 byte, 0x3C expected) on uart_tx_reload_while_busy.v and pass all 13 checks on RTL that ignores start while busy; this has not been run by me.", "Removing the stray 'if (start) hold <= data;' outside the case statement is expected to fix the failure; not verified."], "escalation": null, "notes": "Triage's 30% classification was treated only as a hypothesis. The conclusion rests on the RTL text against its own header contract, together with the reproduced 1-of-4 failure. The repro's sampling assumes inputs change on the falling edge and tx updates after the rising edge, with each bit lasting 4 cycles from the posedge that captures start. A watchdog prints a single verdict line and calls $finish only if the main sequence hangs."}
=== FILE: tb/uart_tx_reload_while_busy_repro_tb.v ===
`timescale 1ns / 1ps
// Repro: a start pulse while a frame is in flight must be ignored (8N1 UART TX).
module uart_tx_reload_while_busy_repro_tb;
    localparam integer CPB = 4;

    reg        clk   = 1'b0;
    reg        rst   = 1'b1;
    reg        start = 1'b0;
    reg  [7:0] data  = 8'd0;
    wire       tx;
    wire       busy;

    uart_tx #(.CLKS_PER_BIT(CPB)) dut (
        .clk(clk), .rst(rst), .start(start), .data(data), .tx(tx), .busy(busy)
    );

    always #5 clk = ~clk;

    integer passed = 0;
    integer failed = 0;
    reg [8*64-1:0] nonce;
    reg done = 1'b0;

    task check(input cond, input [8*32-1:0] what);
        begin
            if (cond === 1'b1) passed = passed + 1;
            else begin
                failed = failed + 1;
                $display("CHECK FAILED at %0t: %0s", $time, what);
            end
        end
    endtask

    task wait_negedges(input integer n);
        integer k;
        begin
            for (k = 0; k < n; k = k + 1) @(negedge clk);
        end
    endtask

    task send_frame(input [7:0] exp, input inject, input [7:0] other);
        reg [7:0] rx;
        integer i;
        begin
            @(negedge clk); data = exp; start = 1'b1;
            @(negedge clk); start = 1'b0;      // start captured on the posedge in between
            wait_negedges(CPB/2);              // middle of start bit
            check(tx == 1'b0, "start bit low");
            for (i = 0; i < 8; i = i + 1) begin
                if (inject && i == 3) begin
                    @(negedge clk); data = other; start = 1'b1;
                    check(busy == 1'b1, "busy during frame");
                    @(negedge clk); start = 1'b0;
                    wait_negedges(CPB - 2);
                end else
                    wait_negedges(CPB);
                rx[i] = tx;                    // middle of data bit i
            end
            wait_negedges(CPB);                // middle of stop bit
            check(tx == 1'b1, "stop bit high");
            check(rx == exp, "received byte equals sent byte");
            if (rx !== exp) $display("  sent %02h received %02h", exp, rx);
            while (busy) @(negedge clk);
            check(tx == 1'b1, "idle line high");
        end
    endtask

    initial begin
        wait_negedges(4);
        rst = 1'b0;
        wait_negedges(2);
        send_frame(8'hA5, 1'b0, 8'h00);
        send_frame(8'h3C, 1'b1, 8'hC3);
        send_frame(8'h5A, 1'b0, 8'h00);
        wait_negedges(2);
        done = 1'b1;
        if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) nonce = "none";
        $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed);
        $finish;
    end

    initial begin
        #200000;
        if (!done) begin
            if (!$value$plusargs("nirmaan_nonce=%s", nonce)) nonce = "none";
            $display("CHECK FAILED: watchdog timeout");
            $display("NIRMAAN-SIM %0s %0d passed, %0d failed", nonce, passed, failed + 1);
            $finish;
        end
    end
endmodule
=== END FILE ===
